The fork retargets the plugin at the DeepSeek Harness 0.2.x plugin APIs:

  * the settings section is no longer registered by the plugin
    (`installSettingsSection` / `settingsNamespace` were removed from
    `@deepseek-ai/dsh-settings` in 0.1.7; forms are now derived from the
    profile entry and its exported `Config`);
  * session persistence is addressed through per-session handles
    (`sessionPersistence.open` / `create` + handle `read` / `append` / `flush`)
    instead of the retired service-level `load` / `append` pair.

See MAINTAINING.md for the exact files and the shipped-build policy.
